('policy_english','The Site collects, stores, processes and discloses your data in accordance with this policy, whether you participate with or without an account. [b]We do not use your data for sales, marketing, or training artificial intelligence models.[/b]\n\n[h2]Data we collect upon registration[/h2]\nRegistering for an account is required to participate in discussions on the Site. We collect the following information about registered users:\n\n[list]\n[*] [b]Username:[/b] Upon registration, you provide a username that is associated with all posts, comments and other actions your account takes on the Site. You may change your username in your Account Settings.\n[*] [b]Email address:[/b] Registration requires your email address, which is later used for email notifications pertaining to your use of the site, and optionally important news about the site. Your email is not displayed publicly, but only to moderators and administrators of the site. You can control your email notifications under your Notification Preferences, or change your email address under Account Settings.\n[*] [b]Profile information:[/b] Your user profile includes many other optional fields, such as your birthdate or pronouns. This information is displayed publicly, and you may change or remove it under Profile Details.\n[/list]\n\nProcessing this information is necessary for the performance of a contract to which you are a party. If you would like to delete your account, you may use the &quot;Delete your account&quot; option under the profile area, or contact us using the link from the footer.\n\n[h2]Data we collect automatically[/h2]\nThe following information is sent to us automatically by your web browser when you access the Site:\n\n[list]\n[*] IP address and geolocation data\n[*] Browser version and type\n[*] Operating system version and type\n[*] Pages that you visit and download on the Site\n[*] Pages that referred you to the Site\n[/list]\n\nWe use this information to combat abuse and address technical issues. This information is not displayed publicly, but only to moderators and administrators of the Site. Unless involved in an anti-abuse measure, this information is automatically deleted after 30 to 90 days.\n\n[h2]Data collected by third parties[/h2]\nWe use NearlyFreeSpeech.NET as our web host, and Cloudflare as our CDN. They describe how they handle your data in their privacy policies [url=https://www.nearlyfreespeech.net/policies/privacy#public]here (NearlyFreeSpeech.NET)[/url] and [url=https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/]here (Cloudflare)[/url]. By continuing to use the Site, you also agree to these policies.\n\nWhile we do not use other third parties to operate the Site, we allow members of the Site to embed content from other sites, namely image, audio and video hosts. These privacy policies can be found on their websites, and this privacy policy not does not cover such embedded content.\n\n[h2]Rights[/h2]\nWe aim to provide you with as much control as possible over the data we collect on you. In case any clarification or assistance is needed, contact us using the link from the footer.\n\n[list]\n[*] To access, update or delete your data, visit your account settings or contact us.\n[*] To request we correct inaccurate or incomplete information about you, please contact us.\n[*] To object to our processing of, request that we restrict the processing of, or request a copy of your personal data, please contact us.\n[*] You may lodge a complaint with the relevant supervisory authority.\n[*] We take reasonable effort to discourage children from disclosing any kind of personal information on the Site, and remove it when we notice it. If you are a parent or guardian aware that your child has provided us with personal information without your consent, please contact us.\n[/list]\n\n[h2]Cookies[/h2]\nCookies we use are divided in two categories: [b]preference[/b] cookies that allow you to customize certain features (e.g. website theme), and [b]authentication[/b] cookies that allow you to access your account on the Site. We do not use cookies for analytics or tracking.\n\n[h2]Sharing[/h2]\nWe may disclose your personal information if we believe that it is required to satisfy a legal warrant, subpoena, court order, law, regulation or other judicial or administrative order in our operating countries.\n\n[h2]Security[/h2]\nThe security of your data is important to us. We use all methods available to us to ensure that it is protected against access, use or disclosure by unauthorized parties. In the event of a data breach, we will inform all affected users, as well as relevant authorities, through private communication or a public notice.'),
